## 3. RAG Status Definitions
RAG (Red, Amber, Green) is used to monitor project health and identify projects that require attention.
Status	Description	Action Required
🟢 Green	Project is progressing according to plan.	Continue regular monitoring.
🟡 Amber	Potential delays or issues have been identified.	Take corrective action and monitor closely.
🔴 Red	Serious issues may affect project delivery.	Immediate action and management escalation.

Proposed RAG Criteria
•	Green: Schedule variance up to 5%, with no critical unresolved blockers.
•	Amber: Schedule variance above 5% and up to 10%, or a significant unresolved dependency.
•	Red: Schedule variance above 10%, a critical blocker, or a credible threat to the agreed delivery date.
These are proposed assessment criteria, not existing company policies.

